      "message": "I think removing this and calling cache_tag_assign_domain() down will cause assigning DEVTLB tags to be missed. We might need to move the cache tag assign to intel_pasid_setup_first_level() under iommu-\u003elock after deriving the ats_supported/ats_enabled from context entry. Same for setup_sl. legacy is not affected as setup_lm_ce passes ats_supported in the hypercall argument. But we should probably move that also to domain_context_mapping_one for parity with this calls.\n\nSo domain refcount remains here in iommu_hc.c, while cache tag handling goes back to iommu.c/pasid.c. On the teardown path that would mean calling `pkvm_get_iommu_domain_noref()` in `domain_context_clear_one`, and `intel_pasid_tear_down_entry` and passing the `domain` back to `pkvm_iommu_pasid_teardown`. Or keep the tear down path as it is, but it will be a slight logical mismatch.\n\nWDYT?",
