      "message": "\u003e A racing teardown operation between intel_pasid_setup_first_level and cache_tag_assign_domain can cause the cache_tag_unassign_domain to not flush DEVTLB there by device retaining the stale entries in its devtlb.\n\nArgh, indeed... So, so long as we don\u0027t have an equivalent of iommu_group-\u003emutex, it seems we indeed have no better option than move cache_tag_assign_domain()/cache_tag_unassign_domain() back to those host driver\u0027s functions (in order to rely on iommu-\u003elock for things it was not meant for).\n\n\u003e We can probably bring back the ats_supported argument back for setup_fl/setup_sl and have pkvm_populate_dev_info_from_ce validate if the host provided values match the values derived from CE. That way, we need not move the cache tag logic to iommu.c/pasid.c\n\nSo it would be \"validate\", not \"populate\"?.. This doesn\u0027t sound better to me, only more intricate.",
